findings.evidence:
Probe: a scratch test file (TestProbeFlowColon) placed with -overlay as internal/config/profile/zz_probe_test.go, run with `CGO_ENABLED=0 go test -count=1 -overlay <scratch>/overlay.json -run TestProbeFlowColon -v ./internal/config/profile/`. It calls parse(..., Options{splitAt: -1|0|3|256}, anyRoot=true) and the public Parse with default Options. Every row gives the same tree at every splitAt and through public Parse, each with diags="" (show() notation):
- "labels: {app:web, tier: db}" -> {labels:{app:s:"web",tier:s:"db"}}
- "k: {port:8080}" -> {k:{port:i:8080}}
- "k: {host:localhost, port:80}" -> {k:{host:s:"localhost",port:i:80}}
- "spec: {endpoints: [10.0.0.1:8080, 10.0.0.2:8080]}" -> {spec:{endpoints:[{10.0.0.1:i:8080},{10.0.0.2:i:8080}]}}
- "spec:\n  endpoints: [10.0.0.1:8080, 10.0.0.2:8080]" -> [s:"10.0.0.1:8080",s:"10.0.0.2:8080"]
- "k: [a:1]" -> [s:"a:1"]; "k: {x: [a:1]}" -> {x:[{a:i:1}]}; "k: {x: [10:30, 11:00]}" -> [{10:i:30},{11:i:0}]
- "{a:1}" -> {a:i:1}; "{a:b}" -> {a:s:"b"}; "k: {a:1, b: 2}" -> {a:i:1,b:i:2}; "k: {a: 1,\n  b:2}" -> {a:i:1,b:i:2}; "k: {a:true}" -> {a:b:true}; "k: {k: v, a:b}" -> {k:"v",a:"b"}
- "k: {a:\"x\"}" -> {a:s:"x"}; "k: {a::b}" -> {a:s:":b"}; "k: {a :b}" -> {a:s:"b"}
- "k: [a:]" -> [s:"a:"]; "k: [a:, b]" -> [s:"a:",s:"b"]
- Controls are correct: {"a":1}, {'a':1}, {a:}, {a:,b}, {url: http://x}.
Reference parsers: PyYAML 6.0.1 (`python3 -I`) gives the YAML 1.2 reading for every row, for example {'app:web': None, 'tier': 'db'}, ['10.0.0.1:8080', ...], {'a::b': None}, {'a :b': None}, {'a:"x"': None} and [{'a': None}] for [a:]. yaml.v3 v3.0.1 from the module cache, run in a scratch module with the cached go1.27.1, agrees on every flow-mapping row ({"app:web":nil}, {"port:8080":nil}, ["10.0.0.1:8080", ...], ["a:1"], {"a::b":nil}, {"a :b":nil}, {"a:\"x\"":nil}, {"a:1":nil}). For [a:] it gives ["a:"], the libyaml behavior the finding mentions.
Root cause confirmed in $GOMODCACHE/github.com/goccy/go-yaml@v1.19.2/scanner/scanner.go:978-995 (scanMapDelim). While startedFlowMapNum > 0, any ':' not followed by '/' becomes a MappingValue. Code check: tokens.go:670-674 calls t.flowColon() (flowcost.go:96-107), which only updates cost bookkeeping and never reads the source character after the ':'. plain.go has no such check, and doc.go does not list the shape. In the vendored suite, the only in.yaml with a plain scalar directly before ':' and ',' is 4ABK ("omitted value:,"), which goccy reads correctly, so no suite case covers the defect.

findings.fix:
In the token pass, while the file has no finding, enforce the shape of a YAML 1.2 flow entry: an optional '?', at most one node, at most one ':', then at most one node, ended by ',' or the closing bracket. Stop the file with RZ-CFG-001 at the offending token in three cases:
(a) a second ':' in one entry (flowColon with top.colon already set);
(b) a node, '?' or ':' that starts after the entry already holds its key and value, with no ',' between them;
(c) a second '?' in an entry that already has its ':'.
`[a:\n b]` and `[? a\n : b]` must still parse. Then goccy never reaches parseMap's column logic inside a flow collection.
Tests: add the five invalid rows above to a flow-shape table at split thresholds -1, 0 and 1, each expecting RZ-CFG-001. Add the ladders (about 1 MiB) and the 80,000-entry comma-less inputs to TestHostileInputsBounded with heap and 2 s assertions, and add them as FuzzLoadYAML seeds.

